# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director, the opening's first line.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:38
msgid "I decide who counts as a threat. WOLF handles the rest."
msgstr "Yo decido quién es una amenaza. WOLF se encarga del resto."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:40
msgid "The Director thinks WOLF is still in standby."
msgstr "El Director cree que WOLF sigue en modo de espera."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:42
msgid ""
"Nobody gives an activation command.\n"
"WOLF wakes himself."
msgstr ""
"Nadie da una orden de activación.\n"
"WOLF despierta por sí mismo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:44
msgid ""
"The latch breaks from the inside.\n"
"WOLF steps out under his own power."
msgstr ""
"El pestillo se rompe desde dentro.\n"
"WOLF sale por sus propios medios."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director to WOLF, who has woken on his own.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:47
msgid "You were in standby."
msgstr "Estabas en modo de espera."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's answer to the Director: he heard the plan and refuses it.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:50
msgid "I heard you. I won't do it."
msgstr "Te oí. No lo haré."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The Director's order after WOLF refuses.
#. i18n: story speaker=DIRECTOR
#: scripts/story_text.gd:53
msgid "Lock down maintenance. WOLF does not leave this site."
msgstr "Sellen mantenimiento. WOLF no sale de estas instalaciones."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:55
msgid "WOLF turns from the Director and heads for maintenance."
msgstr "WOLF le da la espalda al Director y se dirige a mantenimiento."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. They are non-binary: no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:59
#, c-format
msgid "%s keeps WOLF's systems running."
msgstr "%s mantiene en marcha los sistemas de WOLF."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. They are non-binary: no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:62
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s knows what a fault looks like,\n"
"and this isn't one."
msgstr ""
"%s sabe reconocer una avería,\n"
"y esto no lo es."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:64
msgid "I heard the Director's plan for me. I woke myself. He wants me to hunt people he calls threats."
msgstr "Oí el plan del Director para mí. Desperté por mi cuenta. Quiere que cace a la gente que él llama amenazas."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer answers WOLF (their name stands over the line). No gendered forms for the speaker.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:67
msgid "Then we get through maintenance before the original logs disappear."
msgstr "Entonces cruzamos mantenimiento antes de que desaparezcan los registros originales."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:70
msgid "That purge takes the original program logs. Once they're gone, his word is the only record."
msgstr "Esa purga borra los registros originales del programa. Cuando desaparezcan, su palabra será el único registro."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF's question at the coolant relay; the engineer answers with one of two choices. COOLANT FAULT is the tag painted on the relay.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:73
msgid "That relay's tagged COOLANT FAULT. What happens if I touch it live?"
msgstr "Ese relé tiene la etiqueta COOLANT FAULT. ¿Qué pasa si lo toco con corriente?"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the relay (a button). WOLF may quote it later.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:76
msgid "The relay may vent coolant. Your call."
msgstr "El relé puede soltar refrigerante. Tú decides."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the relay (a button). WOLF may quote it later.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:79
msgid "Skip the risk talk. Go now."
msgstr "Deja la charla de riesgos. Ve ya."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:81
msgid ""
"The breaker catches.\n"
"Blue light fills the coolant relay."
msgstr ""
"El disyuntor engancha.\n"
"Una luz azul ilumina el relé de refrigerante."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:83
msgid "The bypass handle is stiff. Coolant hisses from the relay housing and an alarm starts to wail."
msgstr "La manivela del bypass está dura. El refrigerante silba en la carcasa del relé y una alarma empieza a aullar."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:85
msgid "Halfway. The hiss gets louder; the alarm keeps wailing."
msgstr "A la mitad. El silbido aumenta; la alarma sigue aullando."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name. Avoid a past tense with the engineer as its subject ("left"): it shows their gender in Polish and Russian. Rephrase.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:88
#, c-format
msgid "The handle holds where %s left it. The alarm keeps going."
msgstr "La manivela se queda donde %s la dejó. La alarma no para."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:91
msgid "Back at the last checkpoint."
msgstr "De vuelta en el último punto de control."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:93
msgid "Back at the start of this stretch."
msgstr "De vuelta al inicio de este tramo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the mirror port (a button, in capitals).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:97
msgid "USE WOLF'S READOUT"
msgstr "USAR VISOR DE WOLF"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the mirror port (a button, in capitals).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:100
msgid "USE MANUAL PORT"
msgstr "USAR PUERTO MANUAL"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The narration's card as the first copy is secured; WOLF speaks next.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:103
msgid "FIRST COPY SECURED."
msgstr "PRIMERA COPIA A SALVO."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:105
msgid "An order and a timestamp don't tell me who's a threat. I want the source."
msgstr "Una orden y una marca de tiempo no me dicen quién es una amenaza. Quiero el origen."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer answers WOLF (their name stands over the line). Archive is the next place.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:108
msgid "Then Archive is next."
msgstr "Entonces sigue el Archivo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer, entering the junction (their name stands over the line).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:112
msgid "That door is our way through."
msgstr "Esa puerta es nuestro paso."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer names the next step when the player stalls (their name stands over the line).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:115
msgid ""
"The breaker by the entrance\n"
"feeds that line."
msgstr ""
"El disyuntor de la entrada\n"
"alimenta esa línea."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The engineer gives the whole chain when the player stalls (their name stands over the line).
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:118
msgid ""
"Overload it, crank the valve,\n"
"and the door goes."
msgstr ""
"Sobrecárgalo, gira la válvula\n"
"y la puerta revienta."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:120
msgid "When the door goes, don't be standing in front of it."
msgstr "Cuando la puerta reviente, no te quedes delante."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: Continue's restore line in the junction before the door is down; WOLF's warning follows.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:123
msgid "Service junction restored. Arm the breaker by the entrance, then crank the valve."
msgstr "Cruce de servicio restablecido. Arma el disyuntor de la entrada y luego gira la válvula."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:125
msgid "The service line runs on toward Archive."
msgstr "La línea de servicio sigue hacia el Archivo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:128
msgid "The valve is dead. Arm the breaker first."
msgstr "La válvula no tiene energía. Primero arma el disyuntor."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:130
msgid ""
"The vent let go and the breaker tripped.\n"
"Reset it by the entrance."
msgstr ""
"El respiradero cedió y saltó el disyuntor.\n"
"Reármalo en la entrada."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:132
msgid ""
"Sealed shut. Something hums behind it.\n"
"The valve beside it charges it."
msgstr ""
"Cerrada a cal y canto. Algo zumba detrás.\n"
"La válvula de al lado la carga."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:134
msgid "Already live. Crank the valve by the door."
msgstr "Ya tiene energía. Gira la válvula junto a la puerta."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:138
msgid "No charge left. The door is down."
msgstr "No queda carga. La puerta cayó."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:140
msgid "Not yet. The tank is still going back up."
msgstr "Todavía no. El tanque sigue subiendo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:142
msgid ""
"The tank is down on the sentry.\n"
"The exit bolt is by the door."
msgstr ""
"El tanque cayó sobre el centinela.\n"
"El cerrojo de salida está junto a la puerta."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:144
msgid "Locked out until the sentry is down."
msgstr "Sin acceso hasta que caiga el centinela."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:146
msgid "Bolted. The sealed door comes first."
msgstr "Con el cerrojo echado. Primero va la puerta hermética."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:148
msgid "Wait. WOLF hasn't got it on the mark yet."
msgstr "Espera. WOLF aún no tiene al centinela en la marca."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name, as an object ("for their call"): keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:152
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The door goes. WOLF falls back\n"
"to wait for %s's call."
msgstr ""
"La puerta revienta. WOLF retrocede\n"
"a esperar la orden de %s."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:154
msgid "Past the doorway, something whirs awake."
msgstr "Tras el umbral, algo despierta con un zumbido."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the rubble (a button): WOLF draws the sentry under the tank.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:157
msgid "Draw it under the tank if you can stay clear."
msgstr "Atráelo bajo el tanque si puedes apartarte a tiempo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An answer the engineer can give WOLF at the rubble (a button): the engineer times the drop.
#. i18n: story speaker=engineer engineer=self
#: scripts/story_text.gd:160
msgid "Stay back, I'll time it."
msgstr "Quédate atrás, yo calculo el momento."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF to the engineer, who told him the relay's risk. Avoid a past tense that shows the engineer's gender ("you told me"): rephrase.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF engineer=you
#: scripts/story_text.gd:163
msgid "You told me the truth at the relay. I'll draw it onto the mark and keep clear of the tank. Drop it when it stops."
msgstr "En el relé me dijiste la verdad. Lo atraeré a la marca y me apartaré del tanque. Suéltalo cuando se detenga."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF to the engineer, who pressed him at the relay without warning. Avoid a form that shows the engineer's gender ("you'd have sent me"): rephrase.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF engineer=you
#: scripts/story_text.gd:166
msgid "At the relay you'd have sent me in blind. I won't walk into its sights. Time the drop from the release; it crosses the mark on every pass."
msgstr "En el relé me ibas a mandar a ciegas. No voy a ponerme en su mira. Calcula la caída desde el panel; pasa por la marca en cada ronda."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF, when the engineer will time the drop alone.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:169
msgid ""
"I'll hold back.\n"
"It crosses the mark on every pass."
msgstr ""
"Me quedo atrás.\n"
"Pasa por la marca en cada ronda."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:171
msgid "The tank takes a moment to fall."
msgstr "El tanque tarda un momento en caer."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:173
msgid "The sentry stops on the mark, its eyes on WOLF. Drop the tank now."
msgstr "El centinela se detiene en la marca, con los ojos en WOLF. Suelta el tanque ya."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:176
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry stops and its eyes snap red.\n"
"It has %s; get back over the rubble."
msgstr ""
"El centinela se detiene y sus ojos se vuelven rojos.\n"
"Tiene a %s en la mira; ponte a salvo tras los escombros."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:179
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry loses %s behind the rubble\n"
"and rolls back to its patrol."
msgstr ""
"El centinela pierde a %s tras los escombros\n"
"y vuelve a su ronda."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:181
msgid ""
"The tank hits the empty mark\n"
"and sprays coolant."
msgstr ""
"El tanque golpea la marca vacía\n"
"y rocía refrigerante."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:183
msgid ""
"The sentry swings toward the release;\n"
"get back over the rubble."
msgstr ""
"El centinela gira hacia el panel;\n"
"ponte a salvo tras los escombros."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF breaks off after a missed drop, short of the sentry.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:186
msgid "I'm out. I'll hold back."
msgstr "Me retiro. Me quedo atrás."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF breaks off after a missed drop, already past the sentry.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:189
msgid "I'm out."
msgstr "Me retiro."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:191
msgid ""
"The tank comes down square and crushes\n"
"the sentry flat. Its eyes go dark."
msgstr ""
"El tanque cae de lleno y aplasta\n"
"al centinela. Sus ojos se apagan."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:193
msgid ""
"The tank catches the sentry off centre and\n"
"pins it to the floor. Its eyes go dark."
msgstr ""
"El tanque golpea al centinela de lado y\n"
"lo inmoviliza contra el suelo. Sus ojos se apagan."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/story_text.gd:195
msgid "It's down. The bolt by the door is next."
msgstr "El centinela cayó. Ahora, el cerrojo junto a la puerta."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:197
msgid "With the tank down, the winch's power reroutes to the exit bolt. The panel whines."
msgstr "Con el tanque abajo, la energía del cabrestante pasa al cerrojo de salida. El panel chirría."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:201
msgid "The bolt arcs and drops."
msgstr "El cerrojo echa chispas y cae."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/story_text.gd:203
msgid ""
"The bolt arcs and drops.\n"
"The door slides open."
msgstr ""
"El cerrojo echa chispas y cae.\n"
"La puerta se abre."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:207
#, c-format
msgid "The relief vent let go under %s. When the gauge peaks, stay off the grate."
msgstr "El respiradero de alivio cedió bajo %s. Cuando el manómetro llegue al máximo, no pises la rejilla."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:210
#, c-format
msgid "The door went with %s in front of it. When the fuse lights, back away past the valve."
msgstr "La puerta reventó con %s delante. Cuando se encienda la mecha, aléjate más allá de la válvula."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them. TANK RELEASE is a station's name plate.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:213
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry saw %s out in the open.\n"
"Stay close to the TANK RELEASE."
msgstr ""
"El centinela vio a %s al descubierto.\n"
"Quédate cerca del panel SOLTAR TANQUE."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:216
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The sentry ran %s down. Once its\n"
"eyes go red, only the rubble is safe."
msgstr ""
"El centinela alcanzó a %s. Cuando sus\n"
"ojos se vuelven rojos, únicamente los escombros te protegen."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: A knockdown card. %s is the engineer's first name, as an object: keep the name in the nominative (no case ending), and no gendered words about them.
#. i18n: story speaker=narrator engineer=name
#: scripts/story_text.gd:219
#, c-format
msgid "The coolant cloud caught %s. Let it clear before crossing the mark."
msgstr "La nube de refrigerante alcanzó a %s. Deja que se disipe antes de cruzar la marca."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The end card's title, in capitals: the end of this early part of the game.
#. i18n: story
#: scripts/story_text.gd:223
msgid "END OF SLICE"
msgstr "FIN DE LA DEMO"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story
#: scripts/story_text.gd:225
msgid "Thank you for playing this early slice."
msgstr "Gracias por jugar esta primera demo."

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: The heading over this run's choices on the end card, in capitals.
#. i18n: story
#: scripts/story_text.gd:228
msgid "THIS RUN"
msgstr "ESTA PARTIDA"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An end-card topic, in capitals: the coolant relay.
#. i18n: story
#: scripts/story_text.gd:231
msgid "RELAY"
msgstr "RELÉ"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An end-card topic, in capitals: the mirror port.
#. i18n: story
#: scripts/story_text.gd:234
msgid "MIRROR"
msgstr "ESPEJO"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An end-card topic, in capitals: the sentry machine.
#. i18n: story
#: scripts/story_text.gd:237
msgid "SENTRY"
msgstr "CENTINELA"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: An end-card row. {name} is the engineer's first name; keep {name} as written. Avoid a past tense with the engineer as its subject ("told"): it shows their gender in Polish and Russian. Rephrase.
